        {"a": "R-86 (none stated, IN-FORCE derived)", "b": "R-70 (none stated, UNK)", "reason": "R-70 in_force UNK"},
        {"a": "R-88", "b": "any", "reason": "status UNK"}
      ],
      "sensitivity": "If R-95 is derived NOT-IN-FORCE via R-86's issuer rule, then R-86 vs R-95 (both 'none stated', opposite force) FALSIFIES M_status as defined on the stated marker; the model holds only if 'status' means the rule-assigned status (R-95 → PREPARED)."
    },
    "M_adopter": {
      "verdict": "FALSIFIED",
      "deciding_pairs": [
        {"a": "R-81 at issue (adopter none, NOT-IN-FORCE derived)", "b": "R-86 (adopter none, IN-FORCE derived)", "shared_value": "none"},
        {"a": "R-89 at issue (adopter none, NOT-IN-FORCE derived)", "b": "R-86 (adopter none, IN-FORCE derived)", "shared_value": "none"}
      ],
      "undetermined_pairs": [
        {"a": "R-70 / R-95 (adopter none)", "b": "any 'none' state", "reason": "in_force UNK"},
        {"a": "R-88", "b": "any", "reason": "adopter UNK"}
      ],
      "sensitivity": "Rests on coding R-86's adopter as 'none' (not UNK) and on R-86's derived IN-FORCE. If R-86's adopter is UNK, M_adopter becomes UNDETERMINED (none→NOT, Decision Authority→IN otherwise consistent)."
    },
    "M_chain": {
      "verdict": "UNDETERMINED (does not meet the survival condition because M_status is UNDETERMINED; the attribution condition is met)",
      "status_changes": [
        {"ruling": "R-81", "from": "PREPARED", "to": "ADOPTED", "by_actor": "Decision Authority (act: R-86)", "quote": "✅ ADOPTED 2026-08-04 BY THE DECISION AUTHORITY, WITHOUT AMENDMENT (adoption act: R-86)."},
        {"ruling": "R-82", "from": "PREPARED", "to": "ADOPTED", "by_actor": "Decision Authority (act: R-86)", "quote": "Decision Authority confirms and adopts R-81 through R-85 without amendment."},
        {"ruling": "R-83", "from": "PREPARED", "to": "ADOPTED", "by_actor": "Decision Authority (act: R-86)", "quote": "Decision Authority confirms and adopts R-81 through R-85 without amendment."},
        {"ruling": "R-84", "from": "PREPARED", "to": "ADOPTED", "by_actor": "Decision Authority (act: R-86)", "quote": "Decision Authority confirms and adopts R-81 through R-85 without amendment."},
        {"ruling": "R-85", "from": "PREPARED", "to": "ADOPTED", "by_actor": "Decision Authority (act: R-86)", "quote": "Decision Authority confirms and adopts R-81 through R-85 without amendment."}
      ],
      "uncoded_change_note": "R-81 also moved from as-filed (unmarked, summary claiming 'isolation repair ACTIVE') to PREPARED by the ARB Chief's own provenance annotation ('The Chief declines to resolve an ambiguity about the Chief's own authority in the Chief's own favour'); this is attributable to the Chief but was not coded as a separate state."
    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "Only M_issuer is falsified on robust values (same ruling R-81, same issuer, force changes on adoption). M_adopter's falsification depends on coding choices for R-86. M_status is never contradicted by explicitly marked PREPARED/ADOPTED states; it is UNDETERMINED only because two 'none stated' rulings (R-70, R-95) have UNK force.",
    "Most NOT-IN-FORCE values are derived, and the derivation uses the text's own PREPARED→not governing link (R-81, R-86). This makes the M_status test partly circular for R-89; R-81..R-85's NOT-IN-FORCE rests on R-86's 'become governing' wording rather than on the marker.",
    "R-86 itself states the force rule in issuer terms: 'Any future ruling issued by the ARB Chief remains PREPARED, NOT ADOPTED, until the Decision Authority acts on it' — issuer determines default status, adoption act changes status, status gates force: the text's own shape is M_chain.",
    "Cited-only rulings excluded from coding (force presupposed, not stated): R-60, R-66, R-72, R-76, R-79. R-83 is covered within R-81..R-85."
  ]
}

